      "writtenOn": "2017-08-16T04:15:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m wondering if the \"add\" annotation should be more precise. Most of the time, your tool knows that there is a jump at some callsite, that you can resolve to function[file:line], so I\u0027m wondering if the annotation should be made more explicit.\n\nExample:\n\none.c:\n1: void a() {\n2:     blah-\u003einit();\n3: }\n\nWe know that a[one.c:2] calls a function pointer, but we can\u0027t resolve it (so we should throw a warning).\n\nThen, the developer will be able to annotate the callsite, and say:\n\na[one.c:2]\n - my_sensor0_init\na[one.c:2]\n - my_sensor1_init\n\nIf either of my_sensor0_init or my_sensor1_init can be called.\n\nOf course that\u0027d require updating the annotations every time the code is changed, but maybe that\u0027s ok?\n\nWDYT?",
      "revId": "99941406f1e21ac9ab1e8b5c6286d893d3b1b506",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a0a157ad_2df9dbee",
        "filename": "extra/stack_analyzer/example_annotation.yaml",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 11,
      "author": {
        "id": 1230649
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-08-16T05:45:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My concern is actually about updating the annotation file every time the code is changed, because I don\u0027t know how to find and warn the users about mismatching.\n\nBut it will useful after we start to output the warnings about function pointers. At that time, if your annotation doesn\u0027t match the location of function pointer after updating, the function pointer warning will show up again to notify you (if your old annotation doesn\u0027t point to another pointer accidentally).\n\nDo you think I should add this in this CL ?",
      "parentUuid": "0f28e193_39a9000b",
      "revId": "99941406f1e21ac9ab1e8b5c6286d893d3b1b506",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
